            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "For the case when constructed by Iterable, this is easy (though costly).",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "For the case other case - I guess the same thing - when seeking backwards, just go back to the beginning and recount.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "We COULD add options for how to implement seekablity (caching maybe much cheaper - but then you pay when not using the feature).",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "In Stroika v2.0a208 - I switched the BLOB CTOR case from seekable to not seekable (just to save time on above implementation). SB OK - but we;;ll need to test/see.",
                     "type" : "text"
